===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|theosophy|ist}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|en|the|o|so|phist}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# an advocate of, or believer in [[theosophy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|last=More|first=Henry|authorlink=Henry More|chapter=A brief discourse of the nature, causes, kinds, and cure of enthusiasm|page=30, or, § xliv|title=A collection of several philosophical writings|location=London|publisher=Flesher|year=1662|edition=2nd|oclc=|pageurl=http://archive.org/stream/collectionofseve00more#page/n275/mode/1up|passage=What can it be but the heaving of the [[hypochondria|Hypochondria]] that lifts up the Mind to such high comparisons from a supposition so false and foolish? But I have observed generally of [[chemists|Chymists]]{{SIC}} and '''Theosophists''', as of feveral other men more palpably mad, that their thoughts are carried much to [[astrology|Astrology]], it being a fancifull study built upon very slight grounds, and indeed I do not queftion, but a relique of the ancient [[superstition]] and Idolatry amongst the rude Heathens, which either their own Melancholy, or something worse, instructed them in.}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}

